<title>USA: NYSE suspends trading in Sidek's two ADR's.</title>
<headline>NYSE suspends trading in Sidek's two ADR's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Thursday it suspended trading in two American Depositary Receipts representing different kinds of shares in Mexico's Grupo Sidek SA de CV.</p>
<p>The exchange said it halted trading in ADR's representing four shares of Series L Common Stock and in ADR's representing four shares of Series B Common Stock.</p>
<p>&quot;Following suspension, application will be made to the Securities and Exchange Commission to delist the issues,&quot; it said. The exchange said the company had fallen below its listing criteria.</p>
</text>
